Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.01,0:00:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yadmoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.57,0:00:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Yadmoo! Yadmoo! Yadmoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.99,0:00:14.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Yadmoo.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.81,0:00:16.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.55,0:01:07.43,Default,,0,0,0,,That sounded like Serenity.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.71,0:01:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, what?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.13,0:01:11.77,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll make sure she's okay, Serenity!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.29,0:01:13.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.81,0:01:15.47,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got to stick together!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.95,0:01:23.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to say that your friend\Nwill never be the same again.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.57,0:01:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Tristan!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.75,0:01:26.73,Default,,0,0,0,,He's gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.55,0:01:29.07,Default,,0,0,0,,This is all my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.15,0:01:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.55,0:01:32.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Serenity, don't say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.81,0:01:33.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.87,0:01:35.16,Default,,0,0,0,,You gotta stay strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.39,0:01:37.55,Default,,0,0,0,,He lost trying to protect me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.89,0:01:39.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Where do you think you're going?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.95,0:01:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel isn't over, and the\NBig Five need all of your bodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.45,0:01:48.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, it's the female's turn,\Nso make your move already.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.41,0:01:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity, you can do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.41,0:01:51.75,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong, my dear?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.03,0:01:55.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't you duel without your friend\NTristan standing beside you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.91,0:01:58.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't listen to this guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.53,0:02:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity: Too late for that. I\Nthink she's already blown a fuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.05,0:02:05.73,Default,,0,0,0,,She's in no condition to duel. He's right,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.93,0:02:09.47,Default,,0,0,0,,she's in bad shape But I need her\Nhelp to crush this guy Or we're
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.55,0:02:13.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Gonna be stuck here forever. I've\Nruined everything. Thanks to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.69,0:02:14.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Tristan is...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.61,0:02:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Who knows where?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.97,0:02:17.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.88,0:02:20.90,Default,,0,0,0,,we may be able to bring Tristan\Nback But we gotta play our
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.99,0:02:24.99,Default,,0,0,0,,best Now it's time for you to get\Nup Brush yourself off and duel
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.87,0:02:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.91,0:02:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It's no use.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.49,0:02:32.19,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, we'll skip her turn. Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.45,0:02:34.16,Default,,0,0,0,,It makes no difference to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.81,0:02:36.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.72,0:02:40.56,Default,,0,0,0,,This is going to be tricky, but if\Nit works, it could pay off big time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.65,0:02:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I just need a little luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.53,0:02:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Dimension Hole!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.43,0:02:49.19,Default,,0,0,0,,This magic card removes a monster\Nfrom the field for one turn,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.37,0:02:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'm using it on my own monster,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.69,0:02:52.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Assailant.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.67,0:02:56.53,Default,,0,0,0,,So your Machine King loses 100\Nattack points since my Dark
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.61,0:02:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Assailant is no longer on the\Nfield to give him extra power.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.75,0:03:00.93,Default,,0,0,0,,And it gets better.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.27,0:03:02.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Check out this magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.95,0:03:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Play whatever you'd like.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.59,0:03:07.17,Default,,0,0,0,,There's absolutely nothing\Nthat can save you now.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.25,0:03:08.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.83,0:03:10.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Not even this?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.55,0:03:12.69,Default,,0,0,0,,A dice dungeon magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.85,0:03:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't know me, but let's just\Nsay I know a thing or two about dice.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.89,0:03:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,And now it's time for me to\Nroll you right out of this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.83,0:03:23.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I'm changing this\Ncard game into a dice game.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.71,0:03:27.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I activate Dimension\NDice and Dice Dungeon.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.93,0:03:31.45,Default,,0,0,0,,This transforms the playing\Nfield into a dice board.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.63,0:03:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What exactly do you plan to do\Nwith this dice game of yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.21,0:03:37.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll find out soon enough, Nesbitt.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.73,0:03:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,when my high rolling sends\Nyou back to the junkyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.01,0:03:43.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid you'll need a\Nlot more than a few dice
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.43,0:03:46.31,Default,,0,0,0,,to dismantle a superhuman\Nmachine like myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.51,0:03:47.35,Default,,0,0,0,,so make your move.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.43,0:03:51.51,Default,,0,0,0,,For starters, I'll sacrifice\NShiranzo in the 13th grade.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.87,0:03:55.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This allows me to summon a\Nsuperhuman creature of my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.75,0:03:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Meet Orgoth, the Relentless.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.13,0:04:07.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now you no longer have those two monsters\Nto give power to your Machine King.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.25,0:04:12.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means old Tinfoil Pants\Nloses 200 more attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.09,0:04:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,and now that that's out\Nof the way it's time
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.55,0:04:19.15,Default,,0,0,0,,to start our dice game\Nand this is how it's
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.23,0:04:21.69,Default,,0,0,0,,gonna work we'll each pick a monster to
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.77,0:04:24.09,Default,,0,0,0,,step onto the dice board\Nand we'll take turns
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.17,0:04:27.65,Default,,0,0,0,,rolling the die as you\Nwish foolish boy i'll
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.73,0:04:31.07,Default,,0,0,0,,choose my still powerful\Nmachine king and i'll
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.15,0:04:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,place orgoth on the board all right i roll
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.41,0:04:37.77,Default,,0,0,0,,first the die will determine\Nmy monster strength
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.29,0:04:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah! Six, baby!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.85,0:04:44.97,Default,,0,0,0,,That roll doubles its attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.13,0:04:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Not bad at all. Let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.61,0:04:50.91,Default,,0,0,0,,That gives Orgoth a total of 5,000 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.31,0:04:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to see what Machine\NKing's power will be.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.69,0:04:57.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Then commence dice roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.77,0:05:01.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.68,0:05:03.19,Default,,0,0,0,,You rolled a measly one.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.43,0:05:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,That means Machine King\Nloses 1,000 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.27,0:05:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you making these\Nregulations up as you go?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.23,0:05:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Check the rule book.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.53,0:05:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the fun starts.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.25,0:05:14.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Orgoth, prepare for assault.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.27,0:05:20.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Now attack as Machine King with...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.37,0:05:21.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Diamond Blade Strike!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.79,0:05:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,This one's for Tristan.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.27,0:05:32.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodbye Machine King.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.33,0:05:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello Scrap Pile.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.73,0:05:34.95,Default,,0,0,0,,That was pure luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.03,0:05:37.44,Default,,0,0,0,,but your good fortune's about to run out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.03,0:05:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Excellent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.05,0:05:43.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Since I'm acting as my own deckmaster,\NI shall call myself to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.93,0:05:45.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Robotic Knight is now in play.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.11,0:05:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll play a magic card\Nknown as Recycling Plant.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.05,0:05:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,This allows me to revive one of my former\Nmonsters and fuse it together with myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.01,0:06:05.89,Default,,0,0,0,,So, Machine King, Merge with me to\Nform a new unstoppable creature.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.23,0:06:13.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I am now more powerful than ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.63,0:06:19.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what have you done?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.83,0:06:23.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I've merged with Machine King\Nto form perfect Machine King.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.01,0:06:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about it, Serenity.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.97,0:06:27.87,Default,,0,0,0,,He's just a bigger Scrapheat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.03,0:06:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You have no idea of the power I possess.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.53,0:06:33.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I gain an additional 500\Nattack points for every
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.91,0:06:37.23,Default,,0,0,0,,machine on the field But\Nit doesn't stop there.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.39,0:06:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to my clockwork knife magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.79,0:06:42.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I get an additional 500 point boost
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.93,0:06:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,No way he's unstoppable
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.89,0:06:49.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Precisely now prepare to\Njoin Tristan as the next two
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.59,0:06:53.29,Default,,0,0,0,,victims of the big five For\Nwhen I wipe both of you out
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.37,0:06:57.07,Default,,0,0,0,,all of your bodies will belong\Nto us And we can finally
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.15,0:07:02.69,Default,,0,0,0,,escape to the real world Our dice\Ngame is still on, so roll. Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.39,0:07:09.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, a five. That must be good.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.97,0:07:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry to disappoint you, but rolling a\Nfive cuts your attack points in half.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.31,0:07:15.14,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.22,0:07:18.49,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no logic to this\Ndice game at all. No matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.85,0:07:22.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Even with half the strength,\NI'm far more powerful than you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.45,0:07:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Orgoth has only 2,500\Nattack points, and I have 3,850.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.05,0:07:30.39,Default,,0,0,0,,So go ahead and roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.81,0:07:32.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid nothing can save you now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.93,0:07:37.09,Default,,0,0,0,,My die has been good to me so far,\Nso let's see if my luck continues.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.01,0:07:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess not.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.11,0:07:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,One.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.02,0:07:43.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That means my monster\Nloses 1,000 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.91,0:07:45.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And now your Orgoth is even weaker.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.19,0:07:47.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I can blast it away with ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.17,0:07:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And my remaining missiles will blow\Na chunk out of your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.55,0:08:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't let Duke lose, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.97,0:08:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,We need to beat this robot\Nmenace and save Tristan.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.11,0:08:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,But if I try to help, I'll probably\Njust mess everything up again.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.67,0:08:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,So much for your dice-rolling talents.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.41,0:08:17.09,Default,,0,0,0,,With Orgav gone, so goes your dice field.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.21,0:08:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not good.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.57,0:08:21.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Even my best monster couldn't beat him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.53,0:08:26.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Tristan's gone, Serenity's frozen,\Nand I'm fresh out of ideas.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.21,0:08:30.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you mere mortals couldn't stand up
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.19,0:08:32.78,Default,,0,0,0,,to the power of a\Nhigh-tech machine like me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.89,0:08:34.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You're a fool, Nesbit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.51,0:08:36.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You know you're not a real robot.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.07,0:08:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, it's quite sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.99,0:08:41.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Deep down, you're nothing\Nbut a scared little man.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.53,0:08:47.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Soon the rest of the Big Five and I\Nwill return to the life we once knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.13,0:08:51.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Except this time, we won't\Nhave to work under Seto Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.07,0:08:58.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroying Nesbitt's research laboratory\Nwas the smartest decision I've ever made
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.61,0:09:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You've made a terrible mistake today, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.27,0:09:08.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba. That's your opinion,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.57,0:09:10.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Nesbitt I've changed the direction of this
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.89,0:09:13.45,Default,,0,0,0,,company and there was\Nno place for your lab
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.99,0:09:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But sir,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.91,0:09:19.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I've designed all of our high-tech battle\Nvehicles in that lab We make games now,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.55,0:09:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,not vehicles for battle And\Nunless you provide me with
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.67,0:09:25.39,Default,,0,0,0,,an explanation of what you\Ncan offer the new Kaiba Corp,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.47,0:09:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll find yourself\Nwithout a job. This bitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.51,0:09:36.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I spent months developing cutting-edge\Ngaming software for Central Kaiba,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.69,0:09:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,and I hated every second of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.55,0:09:42.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I joined Kaiba Corp to build\Ntanks, submarines, and missiles.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.47,0:09:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Serenity.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.81,0:09:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You've got to get back\Nin the game and help me
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.79,0:09:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,defeat this mechanical\Nmenace for Tristan's sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.23,0:09:52.93,Default,,0,0,0,,This guy can only keep Tristan's\Nbody if he wins the duel,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.13,0:09:55.31,Default,,0,0,0,,so we have to beat him to save Tristan.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.39,0:09:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.30,0:09:58.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I've got you two just where I want you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.51,0:10:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You're down to your last life\Npoints, and she's already given up.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.11,0:10:03.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Victory will be mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.25,0:10:13.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity, I'm begging you to\Nget up and fight this guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.61,0:10:15.73,Default,,0,0,0,,If you don't go right now, you'll lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.81,0:10:22.47,Default,,0,0,0,,That is correct the female must make a move\Nkeep your both together She's gonna go.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.59,0:10:25.35,Default,,0,0,0,,She has two minutes to comply Otherwise,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.69,0:10:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll consider it a forfeit and\Nshe'll join her friend Tristan
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.67,0:10:30.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It's hopeless.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.53,0:10:32.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a sec.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.89,0:10:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I know what may help
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.87,0:10:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity Tristan,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.35,0:10:42.61,Default,,0,0,0,,and I need you just like Joey needs you\Nwhen he duels no one needs me Oh, wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.29,0:10:45.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, my beast can't be stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.03,0:10:47.89,Default,,0,0,0,,So feel his ancient fury.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.59,0:10:53.57,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.95,0:10:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.59,0:10:57.03,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.51,0:10:58.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity, come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.15,0:11:00.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't leave me now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.91,0:11:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I need you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.39,0:11:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't get through this\Nduel without you here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.87,0:11:07.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You're my biggest inspiration, Serenity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.65,0:11:10.47,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother and I never\Ngive up on each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.15,0:11:13.87,Default,,0,0,0,,So why should I give up\Nwhen my friends need me?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.95,0:11:15.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't let them down.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.69,0:11:17.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my move, Metal Mouth.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.91,0:11:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You tell him.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.87,0:11:22.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm coming, Serenity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.59,0:11:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Does Joey even have the slightest\Nidea of where he's going, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.75,0:11:30.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I doubt it, but at this point,\Nhis guess is as good as mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.53,0:11:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, check it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.15,0:11:33.44,Default,,0,0,0,,That could be the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.85,0:11:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.89,0:11:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.97,0:11:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.88,0:11:43.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Up here!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.27,0:11:47.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It's really you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.79,0:11:48.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.19,0:11:50.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Who'd you expect?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.65,0:11:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Yugi. Teya.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.95,0:11:53.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Duke.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.17,0:11:55.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It's good to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.99,0:11:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry to interrupt this touching reunion,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.05,0:12:02.87,Default,,0,0,0,,but I have a duel to win and\Na virtual world to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.11,0:12:05.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Just what we thought. Right, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.57,0:12:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He must be one of the big five.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.51,0:12:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, where's Tristan?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.19,0:12:10.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, wasn't he with you? No.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.41,0:12:13.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Tristan is gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.41,0:12:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,He lost. Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.53,0:12:16.41,Default,,0,0,0,,He lost?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.77,0:12:17.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.07,0:12:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That means... Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.93,0:12:21.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Tristan!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.45,0:12:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,That tin-plated creep is gonna be\Nstrutting around in Tristan's body? No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.49,0:12:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.40,0:12:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,He tried his best.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.61,0:12:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,He was only trying to protect me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.07,0:12:35.07,Default,,0,0,0,,And now we may never get him back.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.71,0:12:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.77,0:12:37.81,Default,,0,0,0,,They need help.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.89,0:12:40.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You should see if you\Ncan enter the duel, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.13,0:12:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,To take Tristan's place\Nand help them. Good idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.31,0:12:47.33,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, make room for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.15,0:12:48.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Negative.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.06,0:12:51.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Intruders are forbidden to duel, Vigness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.07,0:12:53.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, listen up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.03,0:12:56.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever you do, don't give up, Serenity.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.69,0:12:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm here for you, and I\Nknow you can do this. Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.35,0:13:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna be your guardian angel,\Nway up here in the rafters. Got that?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.65,0:13:08.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Now show him what you got, sis.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.35,0:13:11.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Joey. Go get him!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.09,0:13:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,He's all yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.37,0:13:15.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mess with the wheelers, Tin Man.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.71,0:13:19.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid it's too late for all of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.71,0:13:22.33,Default,,0,0,0,,This one's for Tristan.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.33,0:13:24.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Now...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.53,0:13:27.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.55,0:13:31.41,Default,,0,0,0,,As Joey and Yugi would say,\NI have to trust my cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.95,0:13:37.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity, you already know everything you\Nneed to in order to beat this guy. Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.73,0:13:41.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I just have to remember everything\NTristan taught me that day.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.17,0:13:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Tristan,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.53,0:13:47.07,Default,,0,0,0,,do you think that you can teach me how to
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.15,0:13:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,play dual monsters until\Nwe get to Battle City?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.81,0:13:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.67,0:13:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.23,0:13:57.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you know this, but when two\Nmonsters are battling each other,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.09,0:13:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,the one with the highest\Nattack points wins.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.99,0:14:03.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Another rule is that some monsters are so\Nstrong, you can't play them right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.57,0:14:06.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to sacrifice one or\Nmore weaker monsters first.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.03,0:14:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And you can tell how powerful a monster\Nis by counting how many stars it has.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.63,0:14:17.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The more stars that you see in the bottom\Nof the card, the stronger the monster is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.29,0:14:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,There are stars all\Nover the monster cards?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.87,0:14:22.17,Default,,0,0,0,,They must look so pretty, huh, Tristan?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.69,0:14:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, yeah, I guess they do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.99,0:14:26.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And one more thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.51,0:14:28.63,Default,,0,0,0,,You can fuse your monsters together.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.99,0:14:31.70,Default,,0,0,0,,But to do that, you need\Na special magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.81,0:14:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,It's called Polymerization, and it rocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.65,0:14:37.99,Default,,0,0,0,,So, sacrificing and\Npolymerization. That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.61,0:14:39.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.52,0:14:40.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Tristan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.23,0:14:47.57,Default,,0,0,0,,So I have to sacrifice my weak monster\Nto summon a stronger one. Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.85,0:14:51.39,Default,,0,0,0,,that means if I want to summon\Nthe strong monster in my hand,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.47,0:14:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to get rid of my\Nweaker Lady Panther first.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.67,0:14:57.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe this game isn't so tough after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.21,0:14:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,So here goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.35,0:15:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I sacrificed Lady Panther so I\Ncan summon Marie, the Fallen One.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.37,0:15:07.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.15,0:15:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope Serenity's getting the hang of\Nthis, because if she messes this up now,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.69,0:15:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Nesbit will win the duel in his next turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.35,0:15:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I've got the monsters I want.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.47,0:15:24.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I need that Polymerization card so\NI can fuse them together. Serenity. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.53,0:15:25.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Was that you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.73,0:15:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Fear not, Serenity.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.15,0:15:32.93,Default,,0,0,0,,As your deckmaster, I carry with me a\Nvery special ability, the power of fusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.41,0:15:36.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I have the ability to combine\Ntwo or more of your monsters
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.61,0:15:39.95,Default,,0,0,0,,together without the need\Nfor a polymerization card.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.25,0:15:46.19,Default,,0,0,0,,But you must discard one magic card\Nin order to activate my ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.83,0:15:52.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, now feast your eyes on\Nthis little number, Nesbitt.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.55,0:15:54.97,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll dispose of this,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.21,0:15:58.93,Default,,0,0,0,,so then I can activate the\Nspecial ability of my Deckmaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.61,0:16:02.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Fusion vision, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.69,0:16:04.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Got it with the third eye?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.11,0:16:08.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuse together Marie the Fallen One and\Nthe Forgiving Maiden to form St. Joan!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.87,0:16:17.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Impressive, but I'm afraid your monster\Nisn't powerful enough to take me on.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.83,0:16:20.07,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.27,0:16:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,This can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.27,0:16:27.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.37,0:16:29.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Command Angel's special power kicked in.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.97,0:16:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,It raised the strength of every fairy\Nmonster on the field, including St.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.39,0:16:35.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Joan.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.30,0:16:38.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to Tristan's monster card,\Nwe can still do this. Now her St.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.03,0:16:41.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Joan has 3,200 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.47,0:16:45.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but his perfect machine\Nking still has more points. St.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.57,0:16:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Joan needs another power boost.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.03,0:16:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But how can she get that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.71,0:16:50.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Tristan's card!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.65,0:16:52.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, guys! Listen!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.95,0:16:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I know how you can do this, but\Nyou're going to need Tristan's help!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.45,0:16:58.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust me on this!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.83,0:17:00.65,Default,,0,0,0,,How can Tristan help us?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.23,0:17:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,He's not.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.25,0:17:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you guys not.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.53,0:17:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,No more discussion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.99,0:17:06.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Make your move now!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.95,0:17:08.59,Default,,0,0,0,,What's Yugi talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.37,0:17:10.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Ugh! That's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.11,0:17:13.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Tristan still has a card\Nface down on the field!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.05,0:17:15.27,Default,,0,0,0,,It's our last hope!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.51,0:17:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm putting all my faith in that card!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.21,0:17:22.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I activate my Deckmaster's\Nspecial ability. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.57,0:17:25.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Strike Ninja, do your stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.87,0:17:29.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Activate the card Tristan left\Nface down on the field. No.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.81,0:17:32.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I just gotta ditch two cards first.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.31,0:17:35.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And hope that Tristan left\Nus something worth using.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.83,0:17:37.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess it's time to find out now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.15,0:17:39.15,Default,,0,0,0,,This better work.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.29,0:17:40.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Strike Ninja.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.79,0:17:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Raise his face down card.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.41,0:17:56.19,Default,,0,0,0,,He left us rare metal soul! Awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.45,0:17:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like Tristan came through.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.31,0:17:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Too bad for Nesbitt.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.29,0:18:02.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Rare metal soul raises St.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.13,0:18:04.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Jones' attack points by 1,000!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.39,0:18:09.57,Default,,0,0,0,,That's impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.97,0:18:11.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Now their attack points are tied!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.13,0:18:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,What happens? Just watch!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.29,0:18:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, do the honors, Serenity,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.07,0:18:21.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and get rid of this rusty old pile of\Njunk once and for all. All right. Go, St.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.51,0:18:24.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Joan, and attack the\Nperfect Machine King now!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.91,0:18:50.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Since Perfect Machine King was the\NDeckmaster, he automatically loses the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.71,0:18:52.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, way to go, sis.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.29,0:18:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You fools.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.53,0:18:57.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I may be going offline,\Nbut I want Tristan's body.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.25,0:18:59.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.03,0:19:02.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, let him go, you creep. Negative.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.97,0:19:05.44,Default,,0,0,0,,He's my ticket out of this virtual prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.79,0:19:07.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm finally free.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.09,0:19:18.47,Default,,0,0,0,,That mechanical snake in the grass.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.21,0:19:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.05,0:19:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,They have his body.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.81,0:19:26.33,Default,,0,0,0,,And it's my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.97,0:19:28.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity, are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.47,0:19:34.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It's okay, sis. Really.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.75,0:19:38.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, we won the match.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.79,0:19:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Why didn't that bring\NTristan back? I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.97,0:19:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll find him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.71,0:19:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,They took Tristan's body, but\Nhis mind must be here somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.85,0:19:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad we're all back\Ntogether, you guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.65,0:19:52.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Now we just need Tristan.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.79,0:20:00.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.70,0:20:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Where am I?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.67,0:20:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the only one who's competing
